From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a relaunched GPU process gets the screen back

A GPU process that died on a tty took the desktop with it, though the
browser relaunched it:

    GPU process exited unexpectedly: exit_code=134
    failed to take DRM master on /sys/devices/.../drm/card1: -1
    failed to take DRM master on card0: -1

`DrmMaster` (0019) keeps the browser's own `dup` of every card it hands
the GPU process. When the GPU process dies its copy closes and the dup
does not, so the card's master stays open in the browser.
`OnGpuProcessLaunched` then opens the card again: an `open` takes master
only on a card that has none, and `drmSetMaster` on a file that never
had it is EACCES without CAP_SYS_ADMIN. `DrmMaster::Add` logged that,
then replaced the old dup, closing the last master the card had. The
new GPU process drew into a card nobody was master of.

So the browser lets go of every card it held, next to upstream's own
`drm_devices_.clear()`, before it opens the primary card again.

`DrmMasterTest.ADeadGpuProcessCardsAreLetGoOf` covers `ForgetEvery`;
`scripts/test-a-relaunched-gpu-process-gets-the-screen.sh` reads the
series for the call before the reopen.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.cc
index 13fdfa4187..716f83affb 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_display_host_manager.cc
@@ -560,6 +560,14 @@ void DrmDisplayHostManager::OnGpuProcessLaunched() {
   {
     base::ScopedAllowBlocking scoped_allow_blocking;
 
+    // DOMICILE: a GPU process launched AGAIN cannot be master through cards
+    // opened while the dead one's are still held. Those are this process's
+    // dups, and they kept the card's master open after the GPU process that
+    // drew through them died. The `open` below takes master only on a card
+    // that has none, and `drmSetMaster` cannot give it to a file that never
+    // had it -- so with them still held the new GPU process gets the card
+    // without the screen, and the desktop does not come back. See `DrmMaster`.
+    drm_master_.ForgetEvery();
     drm_devices_.clear();
     drm_devices_[primary_graphics_card_path_] =
         MapDevPathToSysPath(primary_graphics_card_path_);
